# A FIXED DEFECT, named after it (Go's `test/fixedbugs`), M-package-layout
# step 2, 2026-09-02 (panel 099).
#
# It lives in `check/` rather than `fixedbugs/` and the reason is measured:
# `fixedbugs/` is walked by the canonical-form check, and a case whose whole
# point is a SYNTAX error cannot be formatted — `heroes fmt` exits 1 on it,
# correctly. Every one of that directory's eighteen cases is an FFI case,
# valid syntax with a semantic mistake. `check/` is where a case with a parse
# error belongs, and six `fixedbugs-*` cases already sit here.
#
# SYMPTOM: two broken `use` lines, **one diagnostic**. This exact text gave
# `module_path_climbs` for line 12 and said nothing at all about line 14 —
# and `heroes check --json` confirmed the second was never produced rather
# than merely not printed. Worse than a missing message: the parser also
# reached **zero** `use` declarations and, on the first shape of the repair,
# could swallow a `function` below them, so a file could lose a declaration
# to a mistake three lines above it.
#
# CAUSE: `use` is not in panel 007's ender list, so the lexer closes a use
# line with a `terminator` only when its last token could END a statement.
# `use lex/..` and `use shapes/` end in punctuation, so **no terminator is
# emitted** — and both new refusals recovered with
# `cursor.recover_to_next_decl`, which scans forward until it consumes one.
# With none on the line, it ran past the end and ate whatever came next. The
# old dot refusal had the same bug and never showed it: `use geom.shapes`
# ends in an identifier, so a terminator existed and the scan stopped in the
# right place. `missing_name` in the same file had already reasoned about
# this hazard by comparing LINE NUMBERS, for exactly this reason, and said so
# in a comment — the repair generalises that reasoning instead of adding a
# third special case.
#
# FIX: `parse_use.skip_rest_of_line` drops the tokens whose line is the use
# line's, so the cursor lands on the next declaration's own first token. A
# line exists whatever the last token on it was, which is what makes it a
# landmark and a terminator not one. Applied to all three punctuation
# refusals at once — the climb, the dangling separator, and the dot form that
# provoked none of it (CLAUDE.md §1: a repair is attacked at the shapes next
# to the one that provoked it).
#
# The unit test that pins the same defect is in `selfhost/module_paths.hero`,
# which is where the parser can be called: `parse_use.hero` cannot reach it,
# because `parse` uses `parse_use` and Heroes refuses module cycles.
use lex/..  #~ module_path_climbs

use shapes/  #~ module_path_wants_a_part

function main()
    print(0)
